title: Party Disunity
new-page: true
is-card: true
view-if: party_disunity_timer = 0 and (dissent >= 0.3 or (pragmatist_dissent > 30 and not pragmatist_resign) or (democratic_socialist_dissent > 30 and not democratic_socialist_resign) or (new_left_dissent > 30 and not new_left_resign) or (trade_unionist_dissent > 30 and not trade_unionist_independent))
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; party_disunity_timer = 4
card-image: img/Reichstagsfraktion_der_SPD.jpg
frequency: 200
tags: party_affairs

# TODO: party dissent events for every faction, have a good image for this... 

= Party Disunity

The party is being torn apart by internal dissent. Upset at the leadership and general direction, factions have started sabotaging their rivals, hampering our efforts to win votes and carry out our policies.

[? if pragmatist_dissent > 30 : The <span style="color: #de6a70;">pragmatists</span> are upset at our direction.  ?]
[? if democratic_socialist_dissent > 30 : The <span style="color: #A52A2A;">*democratic socialists</span> are displeased with the direction of our party. ?]
[? if trade_unionist_dissent > 30 : The <span style="color: #E53935;">trade unions</span> disagree with our present course of action. ?]
[? if new_left_dissent > 30: <span style="color: #94195b;">Leftists</span> are making noises about another party split. ?]

Something must be done to reinforce party unity.

- @enforce_unity
- @concessions_pragmatists
- @concessions_democratic_socialists
- @concessions_left
- @concessions_trade_unions
- @do_nothing


@enforce_unity
title: Enforce party discipline.
on-arrival: pragmatist_dissent -= 8; democratic_socialist_dissent -= 8; trade_unionist_dissent -= 8; new_left_dissent -= 8; workers_spd -= 1; white_collar_workers_spd -= 1

Enforcing party discipline reduces dissent, but it could lead to an exit of dissenting members.

# enforcing party discipline applies to all parties.

# each party has a concessions action and an expulsions action.

@concessions_pragmatists
title: Give concessions to the <span style="color: #de6a70;">pragmatists</span>.
view-if: pragmatist_dissent > 30
on-arrival: pragmatist_dissent -= 10; new_left_dissent += 5

We have promised to adopt a more <span style="color: #de6a70;">pragmatist</span> posture. This may alienate the <span style="color: #94195b;">left</span>, however.

@concessions_democratic_socialists
title: Give concessions to the <span style="color: #A52A2A;">democratic socialists</span>.
view-if: democratic_socialist_dissent > 30
on-arrival: democratic_socialist_dissent -= 10; pragmatist_dissent += 2; new_left_dissent += 2;

We have promised to take more policy suggestions from the <span style="color: #A52A2A;">democratic socialists</span>. Both the <span style="color: #94195b;">left</span> and <span style="color: #de6a70;">pragmatist</span> wings of the party might be displeased.

@concessions_left
title: Give concessions to the <span style="color: #94195b;">left</span>.
view-if: new_left_dissent > 30
on-arrival: new_left_dissent -= 10; pragmatist_dissent += 5

We have promised that we will listen to the <span style="color: #94195b;">left wing</span> of the party. Of course, this leads to increased dissent from the <span style="color: #de6a70;">pragmatists</span>.

@concessions_trade_unions
title: Give concessions to the <span style="color: #E53935;">trade unions</span>.
view-if: trade_unionist_dissent > 30
on-arrival: trade_unionist_dissent -= 10; democratic_socialist_dissent += 5

The <span style="color: #E53935;">trade unions</span> will be granted more influence in party decision making. This upsets the <span style="color: #A52A2A;">democratic socialists</span>, who would prefer to centralize political decision making within the party.

@do_nothing
title: Let the factions argue with themselves.
on-arrival: trade_unionist_dissent += 1; new_left_dissent += 1; democratic_socialist_dissent += 1; pragmatist_dissent += 1

Let the factions bicker; perhaps dissent is healthy for the party.

# TODO: should we be allowed to preemptively expel factions?
